    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i guess. but it feels like you're kind of downplaying the human cost by focusing on \"empirical evidence\" that takes years to show up. if the theory is that it's going to hurt workers, shouldn't we assume the harm is real instead of waiting for a decade of data? it seems like the \"pro-trade\" side always wins the argument just by saying \"wait and see\".",
